  "566 schools in 2024 (Table A): 47 extended classrooms, 331 primary, 33 lower secondary, 65 middle secondary, 88 higher secondary and 2 special institutes. Every dzongkhag’s count here matches the Sub-Total printed in Annexure IV, and they add up to 566.",
  "Thromde (city) schools are counted in their dzongkhag: Thimphu Thromde in Thimphu, Phuentsholing Thromde in Chukha, Gelephu Thromde in Sarpang, Samdrup Jongkhar Thromde in Samdrup Jongkhar.",
  "The Annexure labels about six higher secondary schools as middle secondary, so the split between those two levels within a dzongkhag is approximate; their combined number is exact.",
  "School names are short names as listed in the Annexure (without “Primary School” etc.) and were read from the PDF by text extraction, so some spellings may differ from the printed page. Clearly garbled names were corrected and the extracted form is shown in brackets."
 ],
